 straight up addressing  whether or not he's in spiderman no way  home or will be in the mcu in the future  and listen very carefully to what he has  to say here and listen to how he kind of  stumbles for his words thinking about  what he's supposed to say he's asked how  he feels when he sees his name trending  on twitter and he's asked how he feels  when people break down theories about  him being in spider-man no way home  so i'm not on social media so i don't i  don't i don't have the same awareness  about it as probably other people do but  obviously i hear about it you know my my  my mom will tell me about it and my wife  is aware of it all that kind of stuff  yeah i see it as a massive massive  it makes me feel very grateful that  people care that much  um  you know i  i also like  like it makes i you know i don't i don't  i i wouldn't want to ruin something  either way like yeah do you know what i  mean like so sure  so  it makes me a little anxious in that  regard  you know because  so it's a difficult you know so it's  difficult thing to talk about you know  all i would say is like  i guess  everyone myself included is just gonna  have to wait and see what happens so  when asked about spider-man no way home  he says i don't want to ruin anything  either way meaning he doesn't want to  ruin it if he's in it and he doesn't  want to ruin it if he's not in it but  then he says that it makes him a little  anxious and that it's a difficult thing  to talk about and he says that i guess  everybody himself included is going to  have to wait and see what happens this  is actually rather interesting language  that he's using because if you weren't  returning to the mcu if you weren't  coming back in spider-man no way home  you would simply state that you wouldn't  want to lead people on you wouldn't want  to give them any sort of false hope so  if the answer was absolutely no you  would simply say no this is kind of a  reverse of what andrew garfield has been  doing 